Production boundaries
The implementation deliberately defaults full assessments to referral. It does not bind coverage, calculate premium, issue policies, or automatically approve or decline risks.
Before connecting live data:
Disable demo authentication and mock providers.
Map your actual API payloads to the normalized contracts.
Enforce tenant/entity authorization at the provider boundary; a submitted business ID is not proof of access.
Resolve and lock dependencies in your environment.
Run the included tests plus PostgreSQL recovery, JWT, live-provider, and model integration tests.
Add your existing telemetry, retention, secret-management, and operational controls.
Two limitations are especially important:
Evidence-reference validation rejects invented source IDs, but does not prove that every generated sentence is supported by its cited evidence. Model-generated conclusions still need evaluation and underwriter review.
The package implements a persistent audit timeline, but does not include OpenTelemetry exporters, immutable regulatory archives, historical knowledge-as-of reconstruction, or cross-run conversation caching.
The README documents these boundaries and the exact places to connect your existing application.
